.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
After stepping, a new break\-hit event is generated for the next
command.
The client must call \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] to receive it.
.IP \(bu 2
Stepping into a simple command (no subcommands) is equivalent to
\f[CR]bc_debug_next()\f[R] for that command.
.IP \(bu 2
If the current command is the last in a function or block, stepping
continues to the next command after the block returns (similar to
\f[CR]bc_debug_finish()\f[R] in that case).
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]depth\f[R] field in the break\-hit event increases when
stepping into functions and subshells.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
